.TH DTCODEGEN 1 "2026-11-22" "Amiga UNIX add-on" "CDE"
.SH NAME
dtcodegen \- write C code for an App Builder project
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dtcodegen
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ project .bip]
.RI [ module .bil " ...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dtcodegen
writes the C source of an application designed with
.BR dtbuilder (1),
the App Builder.
For each module named, or for every module of the project when none is
named, it writes
.IR module _ui.c
and
.IR module _ui.h
(the user interface, as Motif calls) and
.IR module _stubs.c
(the callbacks, to be filled in), and for the project a header, the
utilities
.I dtb_utils.c
and
.IR dtb_utils.h ,
and a Makefile.
With no project file named it looks for one holding the modules in the
current directory.
.PP
A
.I .bip
file is a project file, a
.I .bix
file an encapsulated project, and a
.I .bil
file a module, all in the Builder Interface Language that dtbuilder saves.
.TP 16
.BR \-help ", " \-h
print a usage message
.TP
.B \-main
also write the project's file with
.BR main()
.TP
.B \-changed
write only the files whose module has changed
.TP
.B \-merge
merge new
.I _stubs.c
files with the ones already there, keeping the code written into them
(the default)
.TP
.B \-nomerge
do not merge; the old stubs are replaced
.TP
.BR \-project ", " \-p
the project file follows (the default when one is found)
.TP
.BR \-noproject ", " \-np
ignore the project file; use default project settings
.TP
.B \-showall
the application maps all its windows at start-up (the default with no
project file)
.TP
.B \-noshowall
it maps only the windows marked initially visible (the default)
.TP
.BR \-silent ", " \-s
write no messages
.TP
.BR \-verbose ", " \-v
write detailed progress messages
.SH EXIT STATUS
1 for a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dtbuilder (1)
